throw keyword
=========================

throw is a keyword used to explicitly create an exception object and throw that exception to jvm.

throw means - hand over the exception object to jvm.

throws keyword 
=========================
throws keyword is used in the method declaration.

accessmodifier returntype methodname(parameters) throws exception1,exception2....{// method body}

throw vs throws

throw is used to throw an exception.
throws is used to declare and propagate an exception.

throw is written inside the method body.
throws is written in the method declaration.

throw is followed by an exception object.
eg: throw new UserNotFoundException();

throws is followed by exception name.
eg: public void doSomething() throws UserNotFoundException{}

throw will transfer the control immediately to the matching catch or caller.
throws does not itself throw anything,it will just pass the exception onject to the caller.

throw can be used with checked or unchecked exceptions.
throws can also be used to declare the checked or unchecked exceptions.

throw is generally used when our code can detect the problem.
throws is used  when then method doesnot handle exception and lets the caller to handle the exception.

Exception propagation using throws keyword in method declaration.
====================================================================
Exception propagation is the process of passing an exception from the current method to the caller for handling exceptions.

throws keyword in method declaration tells that the method is not handling the exception.

The exception moves up the method call stack until a method handles it by using try catch block
If no method handles the exception,it reaches the jvm 's default exception handler and the program terminates abnormally.

custom exception:
=======================
custom exceptions are exceptions that are created by the developer to handle the specific problem which is not already handled by java predefined exception.

By creating custom exceptions:
	-We can represent application specific problems.
	-we can give a meaningful name 
	-we can handle different problems in a different way.
	-we can seprate bussiness errors from techincal errors.
	-we can provide the additional information about the problem.















































